{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-3596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4x+7}\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-3596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+7 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+({2}^{2}-{2}^{2})+7 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})-4+7 \\\\  & =(x-2)^{2}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4x+7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{(x-2)^{2}+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-2)/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}-4x+7}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+((x-2)/\\sqrt{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}})+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-3596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe7fe31bc155c4d56be66311656a6fb324c7d3386160c1ed4fb94b1bb2b8c492"} {"question" "q-3596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-3596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x-2)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x+2}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-2}{3})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-3596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-49934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-49934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}-18x+6 & =-3({x}^{2}+6x-2) \\\\  & =-3({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+[{3}^{2}-{3}^{2}]-2) \\\\  & =-3({(x+3)}^{2}-11) \\\\  & =3(11-{(x+3)}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above in the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3(11-{(x+3)}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33(1-(x+3)^{2}/11)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x+3)^{2}/11}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+3)/\\sqrt{11})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}}).$  \n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{11}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{-3{x}^{2}-18x+6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+3)/\\sqrt{11})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-49934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe7fe31bc155c4d56be66311656a6fb324c7d3386160c1ed4fb94b1bb2b8c492"} {"question" "q-49934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-49934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x-3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{33}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(x+3)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{11})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{11}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+11}{\\sqrt{3}})+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-49934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{x+3}{\\sqrt{11}})+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-270043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{1-2x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-270043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the argument of the square root in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2x-{x}^{2} & =1-({x}^{2}+2x) \\\\  & =1-({x}^{2}+2x+1-1) \\\\  & =1-((x+1)^{2}-1) \\\\  & =2-(x+1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{1-2x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2-(x+1)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2(1-(x+1)^{2}/2)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{1-(x+1)^{2}/(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse sine:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{2}}).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=(\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{2}}).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-1-\\sqrt{2}/2$ | $-1+\\sqrt{2}/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1/2$ | $1/2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{1+2x-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-1-\\sqrt{2}/2}^{-1+\\sqrt{2}/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-((x+1)/\\sqrt{2})^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}u. \\\\  & =14{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =14\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =14(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =14(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =\\frac{14\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-270043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe7fe31bc155c4d56be66311656a6fb324c7d3386160c1ed4fb94b1bb2b8c492"} {"question" "q-270043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-270043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{14\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-270043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{14\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-348532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{12}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-348532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square for the expression inside the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+15 & ={x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+({4}^{2}-{4}^{2})+15 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2})-16+15 \\\\  & =(x-4)^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given integral, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{12}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x=12{\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{1}{|x-4|\\sqrt{(x-4)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse secant:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}\\,u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x-4).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x-4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $4+\\sqrt{2}$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4+\\sqrt{2}}^{6}\\frac{12}{|x-4|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-8x+15}}\\,\\text{d}x & =12{\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2}\\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{arcsec}\\,u\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =12(\\text{arcsec}(2)-\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{2})) \\\\  & =12(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-348532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe7fe31bc155c4d56be66311656a6fb324c7d3386160c1ed4fb94b1bb2b8c492"} {"question" "q-348532" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-348532" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\pi"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-348553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{\\sqrt{3}-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-348553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+6x+10 & ={x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+({3}^{2}-{3}^{2})+10 \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2\\cdot 3x+{3}^{2})-9+10 \\\\  & =(x+3)^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{6}{(x+3)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x+3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $(x+3).$\n\nSo, let's perform the substitution\n\n$$\nu=x+3.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nLet's use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $\\sqrt{3}-3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ |\n\nFinally, we write the integral in terms of $u,$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{\\sqrt{3}-3}\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}+6x+10}\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =6(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-348553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe7fe31bc155c4d56be66311656a6fb324c7d3386160c1ed4fb94b1bb2b8c492"} {"question" "q-348553" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"} {"question" "q-348553" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\pi"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013818/state.json" "file_sha256" "876fed45d7264d2c84236e4c90aec9c5bd1b86a263ac076e8e2b7f0deed25706"}] "usage" {"q-3596" []} "basis" 1174 "retractions" [[17592186069204 :question/problem "What is $∫\\frac{1}{x^{2} - 4x + 7}dx$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186066756 17592186066757 17592186066758 17592186066759 17592186066760] "immutable_fields" [[17592186066755 :answer-field/correct] [17592186066755 :answer-field/id] [17592186066755 :answer-field/key] [17592186066755 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
